Developed a feedforward neural network from scratch in NumPy to understand backpropagation before using PyTorch. Trained it on MNIST and hit 97.4% accuracy. Then reproduced the same architecture in PyTorch and benchmarked both implementations. Key layer implementation: ```python
import numpy as np

def sigmoid(x):
    return 1 / (1 + np.exp(-x))

def forward(X, weights, biases):
    activations = X
    for W, b in zip(weights, biases):
        activations = sigmoid(activations @ W + b)
    return activations
```
